# Future Architecture: "The Infinite Garden"

To move from "Better" to "Best", we must adopt systems that scale biologically, not just mechanically.

## 1. Fluid Typography (The Water Logic)
Instead of disjointed breakpoints (`sm`, [md](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/edlove-web/README.md), `lg`), we will implement **Fluid Typography**.
This ensures text scales smoothly like water filling a vessel, maintaining perfect harmony at *any* pixel width.

### Implementation Strategy
Use CSS `clamp()` functions in [global.css](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/edlove-web/src/styles/global.css) or Tailwind config.
```css
:root {
  /* Minimum 16px, Maximum 20px, scaling between 320px and 1240px viewports */
  --font-body: clamp(1rem, 0.93rem + 0.36vw, 1.25rem);
  
  /* Minimum 48px, Maximum 128px */
  --font-display: clamp(3rem, 1.57rem + 7.14vw, 8rem);
}
```

## 2. Component Composition (The Lego Logic)
Currently, pages duplicate layout logic. We will move to a **Composition Model**.
Create "Shells" or "Slots" that pre-define the physics.

**Example: `<SanctuaryPage />`**
An abstraction over `Layout` that enforces the constrained width logic automatically.
```astro
<!-- Standard Page Usage -->
<SanctuaryPage title="About">
  <Hero slot="header" />
  <Content />
</SanctuaryPage>
```

## 3. The "State of Grace" (Micro-Interactions)
To feel premium, the site must react to the user.
-   **Scroll-Driven Animations**: Reveal elements as they enter the viewport (using `ViewTimeline`).
-   **Hover Physics**: Elements shouldn't just change color; they should lift, glow, or breathe.

## 4. Internationalization (The Polyglot Core)
[See [localization_strategy.md](file:///C:/Users/Naween/.gemini/antigravity/brain/d017e0ca-5944-4a44-9bc3-eb1960ccaef0/localization_strategy.md)]
We will treat English as just *one* of many interfaces, ensuring the codebase is language-agnostic from the root.
